{"resourceIdentifier":"4841","resourceName":"Ana Primavesi – Sustainable Farming and Restoration Program","description":"Ana Primavesi is an initiative to support the ecological transition in the Atlantic Forest and Cerrado biomes in Brazil. The grouped project has the target of implementing 2 000 hectares of agroforestry and forest restoration over degraded land with small to medium landowners. Supporting agroecological networks and supply-chains, as well as strengthen income and participation of  women and youth. The project will also catalyze natural resources conservation of soil, water and biodiversity, essential for maintenance of life and food security. The program honours a remarkable scientist who inspired the project’s name. Born in Austria in 1920, she was one of the few women at that time to have the title of Agronomist. She moved to Brazil in 1948 where she dedicated her professional and personal life for ‘ecological agriculture’ (agroecology) studies, becoming a pioneer in the country. She taught in Brazilian Universities and became known for her dedication for soil science and its contribution for food production and nature resilience. Primavesi has written many books and inspired many scientists and farm producers. Her legacy teaches about the importance of learning and respecting natural resources as living organisms, nature laws and processes.","location":{"latitude":-21.449083,"longitude":-49.851753},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-12-22","endExclusive":"2024-01-22","endInclusive":"2024-01-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4841"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Atlantic Forest and Cerrado"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Ubá Sustainability Institute"},{"type":"string","value":"Provence, France"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"ty